# Non-secret production switches for scripts/staging_rollout.py --target production.
# One KEY=value per line; blank lines and # comments are ignored.
# The six keys below are all required. The only other keys accepted are the optional CSA_PROD_*
# tuning keys and the optional Jev switches (CSA_STAGING_JEV_SECRET,
# CSA_STAGING_ASSISTANT_DECIDER_*, CSA_STAGING_CUSTOMER_DECIDE_MODE_DEFAULT,
# CSA_STAGING_JEV_FLOOR_*); none is set today. Adding or changing any key is a reviewed PR.
# GATEWAY_MODEL_SECRET names a secret; it never holds a secret value.
# The console and hooks origins and the backup bucket and region are not here (this repository
# is public): they live in /srv/csa-prod/host.env on the instance, with any CSA_PROD_* sizing
# override and CSA_PROD_DB_IMAGE.
# Every switch is on. The workspace assistant needs the gateway's model key, which is the same
# secret file the worker already reads (staging_model_key in the production secret directory):
# it must hold a real key before this deploy. Bookings Calendar and Meet need the Bookings
# calendar callback added as a redirect URI in the Google Cloud OAuth client; Meet needs Calendar.
CSA_STAGING_WORKSPACE_ASSISTANT=true
CSA_STAGING_GATEWAY_MODEL_SECRET=staging_model_key
CSA_STAGING_INVITE_MAIL=true
CSA_STAGING_EMAIL_ASSISTANT=true
CSA_STAGING_BOOKINGS_GOOGLE_CALENDAR=true
CSA_STAGING_BOOKINGS_GOOGLE_MEET=true
